of your partner they think,
"Oh my God, they can leave me.

00:10:24.215 --> 00:10:25.928
"And I might, I'm going
to have to do this first."

00:10:25.928 --> 00:10:27.426
And so they put their finger on the button

00:10:27.426 --> 00:10:29.720
and then all it takes is
enough times of doing that,

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:30.651
enough years of doing that

00:10:30.651 --> 00:10:32.308
and one day somebody will push the button.

00:10:32.308 --> 00:10:34.501
If you are committed to
the relationship you're in,

00:10:34.501 --> 00:10:36.128
bend for life.

00:10:36.128 --> 00:10:36.961
- [Sage] Yes.

00:10:36.961 --> 00:10:38.693
- For multiple lifetimes, for those of you

00:10:38.693 --> 00:10:40.040
who are going to some
back six and seven times,

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:41.341
like some of the people here did.

00:10:41.341 --> 00:10:44.170
You bend, for multiple lifetimes.

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:47.533
I will never, ever, ever threaten.

00:10:47.533 --> 00:10:49.913
Never, neither of you
ever threatens to leave.

00:10:49.913 --> 00:10:51.827
If you threaten to leave,
relationships over.

00:10:51.827 --> 00:10:52.660
It might take three more years,

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.671
five more, 10 years, but its over.

00:10:54.671 --> 00:10:56.613
If you want to be in a
relationship with this person,

00:10:56.613 --> 00:11:00.088
don't ever, ever, ever threaten.

00:11:00.088 --> 00:11:03.035
If you did it before,
it's off limits forever.

00:11:03.035 --> 00:11:05.024
No exceptions, doesn't
matter how mad you are,

00:11:05.024 --> 00:11:07.880
angry you are, sad you are, never.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:09.272
You're not unconscious with your language

00:11:09.272 --> 00:11:11.707
and unconscious with your deeds,
you're aware of the impact

00:11:11.707 --> 00:11:13.321
and you correct it immediately.

00:11:13.321 --> 00:11:14.517
You constantly realize,

00:11:14.517 --> 00:11:17.401
"I'm pissed off, I'm hurt,
I'm sad, its about me.

00:11:17.401 --> 00:11:20.363
"Let me step out of me, I'm
into something bigger here."

00:11:20.363 --> 00:11:22.603
Right? I'm not about that,
I'm about something bigger.

00:11:22.603 --> 00:11:24.506
It's what do they need, let me step out,

00:11:24.506 --> 00:11:26.942
and you do that enough
times, it'll become a habit.

00:11:26.942 --> 00:11:31.706
Then finally number five, the
discipline of giving freedom.

00:11:31.706 --> 00:11:32.956
Giving freedom.

00:11:34.337 --> 00:11:37.767
Men live for freedom, women need it also.

00:11:37.767 --> 00:11:40.105
But it comes in different
forms and it's the power of

00:11:40.105 --> 00:11:42.398
forgiving, forgetting, and flooding.

00:11:42.398 --> 00:11:46.032
Forgiving, forgetting and flooding.

00:11:46.032 --> 00:11:49.360
Now women seem to have more of
a difficulty with forgetting.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:51.262
(audience laughs)

00:11:51.262 --> 00:11:53.929
But, you can be forgiving.

00:11:53.929 --> 00:11:56.379
And forgiveness is when you realize

00:11:56.379 --> 00:11:58.642
that what you thought
happened, didn't really happen.

00:11:58.642 --> 00:12:02.125
You gave it a meaning that
doesn't really match reality.

00:12:02.125 --> 00:12:03.262
You're expecting your partner

00:12:03.262 --> 00:12:05.675
to be something different than they are.

00:12:05.675 --> 00:12:07.211
Flooding is one of the
most valuable skills

00:12:07.211 --> 00:12:08.920
you can do in your life.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:10.197
If you don't flood,

00:12:10.197 --> 00:12:12.672
you'll have a hard time
forgiving and forgetting.

00:12:12.672 --> 00:12:14.476
- [Sage] And we flood our
magic moments, I mean--

00:12:14.476 --> 00:12:15.309
- [Tony] All the time.

00:12:15.309 --> 00:12:16.851
- All the time, and we capture them.

00:12:16.851 --> 00:12:18.589
You know, we have our
little app of a journal

00:12:18.589 --> 00:12:21.077
that we capture all of our,
just our beautiful moments.

00:12:21.077 --> 00:12:23.490
After this event, when
we get home on Sunday,

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:25.674
we'll spend an hour and just
capture all the beautiful

00:12:25.674 --> 00:12:26.563
moments that happened here.

00:12:26.563 --> 00:12:28.205
Everything that was funny,
everything that was beautiful,

00:12:28.205 --> 00:12:29.622
everything that was touching.

00:12:29.622 --> 00:12:31.421
'Cuz otherwise, it's just,
it's actually what Nicole

00:12:31.421 --> 00:12:33.602
was talking about, 'member
she talked about framing?

00:12:33.602 --> 00:12:34.722
You have a peak experience

00:12:34.722 --> 00:12:36.387
and you actually give words to it,

00:12:36.387 --> 00:12:39.168
and that frames it and it
helps to get to that place.

00:12:39.168 --> 00:12:40.878
It's just like, you bypass all that effort

00:12:40.878 --> 00:12:41.726
that took you there,

00:12:41.726 --> 00:12:43.690
and then that's you're
next starting point.

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:45.294
And then you have another peak experience,

00:12:45.294 --> 00:12:46.655
and then you share that and you frame it,

00:12:46.655 --> 00:12:48.547
and you give language
and you give words to it.

00:12:48.547 --> 00:12:50.845
And then boom, you set the bar higher.

00:12:50.845 --> 00:12:54.634
A lot of times what happens
is, we, magic happens in life.

00:12:54.634 --> 00:12:57.880
Grace pours, and we
don't give words to it.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.612
We don't celebrate it,
we don't recognize it,

00:12:59.612 --> 00:13:01.706
we don't see it, we don't appreciate it.

00:13:01.706 --> 00:13:04.395
In putting words to that, of appreciation

00:13:04.395 --> 00:13:08.766
and reliving and experiencing
it, it is, I would say

00:13:08.766 --> 00:13:11.789
it's one of the top 10 things
for us that we do that just,

00:13:11.789 --> 00:13:15.376
it ignites that feeling, and
just of utter appreciation

00:13:15.376 --> 00:13:16.440
and we always capture it,

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.206
so we can always go back and read it.

00:13:18.206 --> 00:13:19.446
It's so beautiful.

00:13:19.446 --> 00:13:21.935
- [Sage] Okay. This is something to share.

00:13:21.935 --> 00:13:23.435
So when we first--

00:13:24.289 --> 00:13:25.540
- [Tony] Its called a set up.
- [Sage] ... it's true.

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:28.137
He was so, oh my gosh,

00:13:28.137 --> 00:13:30.970
like I mean rigid, militant, blue.

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:34.800
Like so intense about these things, and so

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:36.809
anytime that anybody
would talk about eggs,

00:13:36.809 --> 00:13:39.418
he was just like, and did what
felt like he was not vicious,

00:13:39.418 --> 00:13:41.502
but it felt like that level of intensity.

00:13:41.502 --> 00:13:43.299
And so, we were together

00:13:43.299 --> 00:13:45.772
and I was feeling like
I needed more protein,

00:13:45.772 --> 00:13:47.360
and we share everything.

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:50.236
And it was so crazy 'cuz
I started to eat eggs

00:13:50.236 --> 00:13:51.511
and I literally, and I didn't tell him--

00:13:51.511 --> 00:13:52.537
- [Tony] Oh my God!

00:13:52.537 --> 00:13:55.140
- No this sounds nuts,
but I did not tell him

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:57.363
and I felt like I was having
a fricken affair with an egg.

00:13:57.363 --> 00:14:00.317
And I would literally go into the pantry

00:14:00.317 --> 00:14:02.710
and I'd eat the eggs and
I'm like, "This is nuts."

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:05.596
Like this is just crazy,
it seems ridiculous.

00:14:05.596 --> 00:14:09.096
("Chicken Dance" playing)

00:14:10.505 --> 00:14:13.467
- [Sage] (laughing) And I (laughing) ...

00:14:13.467 --> 00:14:17.061
And it sounds nutty,
but I put so much energy

00:14:17.061 --> 00:14:20.969
into hiding my egg eating
and then it got to the day

00:14:20.969 --> 00:14:23.903
when I was like this is
outrageous, this is out of hand.

00:14:23.903 --> 00:14:25.701
And I sat him down.

00:14:25.701 --> 00:14:26.960
- [Tony] So she finally came out---

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:27.793
- Finally told him.

00:14:27.793 --> 00:14:28.626
- [Tony] She shared with me

00:14:28.626 --> 00:14:30.000
the affair she'd been having with eggs.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.217
(Sage and audience laughs)

00:14:31.217 --> 00:14:33.050
And I was crestfallen.

00:14:35.086 --> 00:14:35.919
- [Sage] It's crazy.

00:14:35.919 --> 00:14:36.919
- I still hate them.

00:14:36.919 --> 00:14:37.752
- [Sage] He does.

00:14:37.752 --> 00:14:38.927
- [Tony] I still hate 'em.

00:14:38.927 --> 00:14:41.560
- And I still eat them (laughing).

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.521
I really love breakfast.

00:14:43.521 --> 00:14:46.013
I love my eggs and I love
my breakfast and he's--

00:14:46.013 --> 00:14:46.846
- [Tony] I love her.

00:14:46.846 --> 00:14:49.189
So I love an egg eater,
now you know the truth.

00:14:49.189 --> 00:14:50.272
- [Sage] Yup.

00:14:52.181 --> 00:14:54.493
- So we disagree completely,

00:14:54.493 --> 00:14:56.068
but we love each other.

00:14:56.068 --> 00:14:58.498
So that's how you balance
it out, you get it?

00:14:58.498 --> 00:14:59.924
You get it?

00:14:59.924 --> 00:15:01.775
You put love first.

00:15:01.775 --> 00:15:03.623
You love more than your rules.

00:15:03.623 --> 00:15:05.213
And it makes you a better human being,

00:15:05.213 --> 00:15:06.204
because it opens you up,

00:15:06.204 --> 00:15:07.935
because lots of things
were making life and death

00:15:07.935 --> 00:15:09.276
that really aren't.

00:15:09.276 --> 00:15:10.109
They really aren't.

00:15:10.109 --> 00:15:11.314
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:11.314 --> 00:15:12.263
I hope you enjoyed.

00:15:12.263 --> 00:15:14.193
I'd love to know what did
you think of this video?

00:15:14.193 --> 00:15:16.469
Is there something that you're
going to immediately apply

00:15:16.469 --> 00:15:19.160
somehow to your life, after watching it?

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:21.024
And again, thank you for joining me on the

00:15:21.024 --> 00:15:22.679
Believe Love Series.

00:15:22.679 --> 00:15:24.937
It was a fun ride while it lasted.

00:15:24.937 --> 00:15:26.573
You can go back and watch the other videos

00:15:26.573 --> 00:15:29.600
in this series as well,
and it's sad that its over.

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:32.269
But I'm looking forward to
bringing you something new,

00:15:32.269 --> 00:15:35.486
as a test experiment,
and see what you think.

00:15:35.486 --> 00:15:36.800
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:37.989
I believe in you.

00:15:37.989 --> 00:15:40.086
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:15:40.086 --> 00:15:42.434
and whatever your one word is.

00:15:42.434 --> 00:15:44.851
Much love, I'll see you soon.

